From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 04:39:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The sign-in button opens Office's own sign-in now, and
 nothing aborts on the way.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Clicking 「登录或创建帐户」 in Word did nothing for two minutes and then took
Word down with it.  Two missing exports, one hiding behind the other.

vcruntime140.__C_specific_handler_noexcept was a stub, and calling a stub
aborts the thread.  WebView2's in-process client DLL uses it as its language
handler, so every attempt to bring the environment up died inside the unwinder
and was retried: thousands of "unimplemented function" lines, an env-creation
loop, no msedgewebview2 ever.  The native runtime has it as a separate function
from __C_specific_handler (RVA 0xf270 vs 0xf4c0 in Office's own copy) whose
first instruction is a call to __C_specific_handler; it then terminates when
the answer was ExceptionContinueSearch, the code is 0xE06D7363 and no unwind
flag is set -- a C++ exception escaping a noexcept frame.  That is what this
implements, shared by the x86_64, aarch64 and arm handlers.  ucrtbase exports
it and vcruntime140 forwards, which is how the real pair is arranged too.

With the aborts gone the exception underneath them was visible: 0xC06D007F,
the delay loader's "procedure not found", raised out of mso30win32client.
The code says the module loaded and the export did not exist, which narrowed
it to one candidate -- USER32.CalculatePopupWindowPosition, commented out as a
stub in user32.spec and a stub syscall in win32u.  It is the placement
arithmetic TrackPopupMenuEx does, so it lives next to the menu code: align to
the anchor, step off the exclude rectangle along the axis the caller did not
ask to keep, and stay on the monitor.  TPM_WORKAREA was missing from winuser.h
as well.  tools/popupprobe checks the ten cases directly.

make_specfiles also noticed slc.spec still stubbing what sppc now implements;
slc forwards to sppc on Windows, so let it.

Word survives the click, WebView2 starts as a full browser tree, and the window
that appears is OneAuthWebView2Browser hosting a page titled "Sign in" with a
TLS connection open to Microsoft.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0497a608a3b81bb88de674dfb9b15d6ffa5f3e4b)

diff --git a/dlls/msvcrt/except.c b/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
index b70d74e5f69..d698beb5ce9 100644
--- a/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
+++ b/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
@@ -1097,6 +1097,22 @@ int* CDECL __processing_throw(void)
 } while(0)
 
 LONG __C_ExecuteExceptionFilter( EXCEPTION_POINTERS *ptrs, void *frame, PEXCEPTION_FILTER filter, BYTE *nonvolatile );
+
+/* Shared tail of the __C_specific_handler_noexcept variants: the guarded function
+ * is declared noexcept, so a C++ exception that found no handler in this frame is
+ * not allowed to propagate any further.  Matches the native runtime, which only
+ * looks at the exception code and skips the check while unwinding. */
+static EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION handle_noexcept_escape( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION disp )
+{
+    if (disp == ExceptionContinueSearch && rec->ExceptionCode == CXX_EXCEPTION &&
+        !(rec->ExceptionFlags & (EXCEPTION_UNWINDING | EXCEPTION_EXIT_UNWIND |
+                                 EXCEPTION_TARGET_UNWIND | EXCEPTION_COLLIDED_UNWIND)))
+    {
+        ERR( "C++ exception escaping a noexcept function, terminating\n" );
+        terminate();
+    }
+    return disp;
+}
 #endif
 
 #if defined(__aarch64__)  || defined(__arm64ec__)
@@ -1178,6 +1194,17 @@ EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION WINAPI __C_specific_handler( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *
 
 #ifdef __arm64ec__
 #undef __C_specific_handler
+#else
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *		__C_specific_handler_noexcept   (ucrtbase.@)
+ */
+EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION WINAPI __C_specific_handler_noexcept( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *frame,
+                                                            ARM64_NT_CONTEXT *context,
+                                                            DISPATCHER_CONTEXT_ARM64 *dispatch )
+{
+    return handle_noexcept_escape( rec, __C_specific_handler( rec, frame, context, dispatch ) );
+}
 #endif
 
 #endif /* __aarch64__ || __arm64ec__ */
@@ -1254,6 +1281,15 @@ EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION WINAPI __C_specific_handler( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *
     return ExceptionContinueSearch;
 }
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *		__C_specific_handler_noexcept   (ucrtbase.@)
+ */
+EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION WINAPI __C_specific_handler_noexcept( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *frame,
+                                                            CONTEXT *context, DISPATCHER_CONTEXT *dispatch )
+{
+    return handle_noexcept_escape( rec, __C_specific_handler( rec, frame, context, dispatch ) );
+}
+
 #endif /* __arm__ */
 
 #ifdef __x86_64__
@@ -1334,4 +1370,13 @@ EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION WINAPI __C_specific_handler( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *
     return ExceptionContinueSearch;
 }
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *		__C_specific_handler_noexcept   (ucrtbase.@)
+ */
+EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION WINAPI __C_specific_handler_noexcept( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *frame,
+                                                            CONTEXT *context, DISPATCHER_CONTEXT *dispatch )
+{
+    return handle_noexcept_escape( rec, __C_specific_handler( rec, frame, context, dispatch ) );
+}
+
 #endif /* __x86_64__ */
